<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i+1));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i+1));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that for every position `i` greater than the removed index and less than the old size of the list minus one, the current value at position `i` equals the old value at position `i+1`. This reflects the requirement that the elements shift down correctly after the removal.
